sc: LOK places a new chart off drawings, mirrored, and fast

Patch 0041 puts a new chart in empty cells beside its data. Three
defects remained (Ely R2.10):

- On a right-to-left sheet the anchor was the cell's mirrored top
  left, so the chart reached back over the data and off the sheet.
  The chart now ends at the cell's start there.
- Only cell contents and merges counted as taken; a second chart
  landed on the first. Every object on the target page now holds
  the cells under its bounds.
- The scans stepped one chart size at a time and tested each cell
  run; a sheet with one 100x25 gap off that grid was refused after
  27 s, a full sheet after 73 s. Each scan now jumps past what
  blocked it: by binary search to the last blocked index, and down
  a column by merge runs and drawings, read from the attribute runs
  rather than by walking to a merge's origin. Filled cells are
  stepped with the same test that calls a cell taken, so hidden rows
  and comment-only cells hide no room; each column's run is kept.
